  "reason": "The best result so far is config_049 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 accuracy. Strong evidence across 9 experiments shows scvi_n200 is the dominant RNA encoder, multiprofile far outperforms singleprofile, and transformer aggregation exceeds avgpool. The remaining untested scvi_n200/multiprofile/imagenet_vit_l configuration is config_015 (avgpool, concat), which is the closest untested variant to the best-performing setup. While transformer+weighted is clearly superior, testing avgpool+concat completes the 2×2 aggregation×fusion grid for the top encoder pair, reducing residual uncertainty about whether any interaction between aggregation and fusion could shift performance. As the final experiment, this is the highest-expected-accuracy untested option and the most informative completion of the design space around the current best."
}

